# Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what git tracks.
#
# Allowlist, not a denylist, and the reason is rule 3 rather than image size.
# Nothing that keeps CLAUDE.md, .claude/, the LIBEX_*.md operating docs and
# the knowledge base out of version control is visible to Docker: that
# enforcement lives in .git/info/exclude, which the daemon does not read. A
# denylist would therefore protect exactly the files someone remembered to
# list on the day they wrote it, and every operating doc added afterwards
# would ship. The published image goes to two public registries, so a stray
# local file reaching it is not recoverable by deleting it afterwards.
#
# .env is here for the same structural reason and is the more immediate one:
# it holds real credentials, sits in the repo root, and `COPY . .` would bake
# it into a layer.
#
# CI has never shipped any of this, because it builds from a git checkout
# where those files do not exist. That makes today's published image safe by
# accident. This file makes it safe by construction, and closes the gap for a
# local `docker build` -- which, before this, copied .env, every Claude
# operating doc, .venv, .git, scrapers/ and the 2.1GB apk-work/ into the
# image.
#
# The admitted set below is `git ls-files` at the top level, minus tests/
# and the CI-only tooling files -- requirements-tooling.txt and its lock
# are installed by the workflow, never by the image.
*

!.env.example
!.github/
!.gitignore
!CHANGELOG.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!Dockerfile
!LICENSE
!PRIVACY.md
!README.md
!SECURITY.md
!alembic.ini
!app/
!constraints.txt
!docker-compose.yml
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!migrations/
!pytest.ini
!requirements-dev.lock
!requirements-dev.txt
!requirements.lock
!requirements.txt
!scripts/

# tests/ is deliberately NOT admitted. Nothing ever ran it from inside the
# image: tests.yml runs pytest on the runner against the checkout, and
# publish.yml only builds and pushes, gated on tests.yml having already
# passed. The test runner itself was removed from the image in the same slice
# that added this line, so shipping the tests without pytest would have left
# 952K of code the image cannot execute.

# Re-excluded after the admissions above, since these live inside admitted
# directories and are untracked build or tooling residue. app/static/docs is
# fetched during the build by fetch_docs_assets.sh and checksum-verified
# there, so a copy of it from the build host would be overwritten anyway --
# and must not be trusted in the meantime.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
app/static/docs/
